{
  "version": 1,
  "_note": "The .dsxreport envelope - proposals/live-logs.md 3.6. Canonical bytes are EXACTLY JSON with keys sorted by code point, no whitespace, minimal escaping (\\\" \\\\ \\b \\f \\n \\r \\t, other controls as \\u00xx), unicode raw, SAFE integers only - |n| <= 2^53-1 (a non-integer or unsafe number is refused). The receipt hash is sha256 over the canonical bytes of the envelope WITHOUT its receipt key; the sealed text is the canonical bytes WITH it. The verifier's verdicts are the support macro: not_report (the AI-fabricated paste dies here), modified (edited after export), genuine (hash verifies); assertion reports whether a receipt.integrity attestation rides the seal - verifying THAT is the relay/platform's job (Apple/Google trust anchors), never this core's. Twins: TS packages/kernel/src/livelogs.ts - Kotlin :core LiveLogs.kt - Swift Engine/iOS/LiveLogs.swift.",
